        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-24T14:12:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, the certificate chain in [1] is generated in Keymint, so the leaf certificate does not originate from RKP, but from Keymint.\n\nThe RKP certificate is the second certificate in the chain and it contains the following extensions:\n```\n    X509v3 extensions:\n            ...\n            X509v3 Key Usage: critical\n                Certificate Signing\n            X509v3 Basic Constraints: critical\n                CA:true\n            Android RKP Information:\n                a1:...\n```\nThe key usage is set to `Certificate Signing`. In our case, we will not have the Keymint certificate; we will only be extending the RKP certificate.",
      "parentUuid": "5e125e0e_6aa4fad4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "9cd45f53fe79b98aad290a70c1ba6284382adb1b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
